---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
	{id: 'execution', label: 'Execution model'},
	{id: 'constraint', label: 'Type-correct ≠ valid'},
	{id: 'families', label: 'Five families'},
	{id: 'session', label: 'Session lifecycle'},
	{id: 'funding', label: 'Friendbot & keypairs'},
	{id: 'router', label: 'Invoke / poll'},
	{id: 'modules', label: 'Modules'},
	{id: 'fixtures', label: 'Fixtures'},
];
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Chaos Monkey"
	eyebrow="[ 05 · FUZZ ]"
	description="Type-aware fuzzing for Soroban — not random dumb bytes. Simulate first; broadcast only when preflight proceeds."
>
	<Toc items={toc} />

	<p>
		Full attack-label catalog (math labels, admin patterns, sequences):{' '}
		<a href={withBase('/vectors')}>Attack vectors reference</a>.
	</p>

	<Callout type="warn" title="Real Testnet transactions">
		<p>
			Vectors whose simulation succeeds are signed with an ephemeral Friendbot-funded
			keypair and submitted on-chain. Keypairs are never written to disk or logged.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="execution">Execution model</h2>
	<pre><code>vector → simulate (preflight)
           ├─ simulation fails    → classify from diagnostic events (nothing sent)
           └─ simulation succeeds → sign → broadcast → poll → classify</code></pre>

	<p>
		Many findings are therefore classified <em>without</em> an on-chain transaction. Only
		broadcast txs appear in verification samples and explorer links.
	</p>

	<h2 id="constraint">Design constraint</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>Type-correct ≠ semantically valid.</strong> A random <code>Address</code> is not
		a funded account, token, or authorized signer. Kuyfi classifies conservatively and treats
		ambiguity as ambiguity — see <a href={withBase('/findings')}>Findings</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="families">Five vector families</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Family</th>
				<th>Module</th>
				<th>What it probes</th>
				<th>expectedToFail</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Math / boundary</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_math.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Per-type boundaries (<code>ZERO</code>, <code>MAX_I128</code>, empty/oversized
					bytes/strings, recursive UDT fields one-at-a-time).
				</td>
				<td><code>false</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Authorization</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_access.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					<code>UNAUTHORIZED_CALL</code>, <code>REINIT_ATTACK</code>,
					<code>SELF_CALL_ATTACK</code>, <code>UNAUTHORIZED_ADDR_CALL</code>.
				</td>
				<td><code>true</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Fee / BPS</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_fee.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					<code>BPS_*</code> + type max on fee-shaped numeric params.
				</td>
				<td><code>false</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Liquidity ratio</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_liquidity.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Paired extremes on swap/reserve-shaped functions.
				</td>
				<td><code>false</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Call ordering</td>
				<td><code>fuzzer_call_order.ts</code></td>
				<td>
					Same function twice: reinit / withdraw / claim sequences (once per session).
				</td>
				<td><code>false</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="session">Session lifecycle (<code>runChaosMonkey</code>)</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Generate ephemeral keypair + Friendbot fund + on-chain confirmation.</li>
		<li>Connect Testnet RPC.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Per discovered function</strong>, in this order: math → access → fee →
			liquidity (each self-gates on name/params).
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Once per session</strong> (after all per-function work): call-ordering
			candidates.
		</li>
		<li>
			Aggregate <code>ChaosReport</code> —
			<code>SECURE</code> / <code>PRECONDITION_FAIL</code> filtered from findings list,
			kept in counters.
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p>
		Progress strings include stages like generating the ephemeral keypair and per-function
		family lines (math / access / …) via the progress callback.
	</p>

	<h2 id="funding">Friendbot &amp; ephemeral keypairs</h2>
	<p>Module <code>keypair_factory.ts</code>:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Friendbot URL: <code>https://friendbot.stellar.org/?addr=</code></li>
		<li><strong>3</strong> funding retries with backoff between attempts</li>
		<li>
			After HTTP OK: poll <code>getAccount</code> up to <strong>10 × 1s</strong> for
			on-chain confirmation
		</li>
		<li>
			Failure after retries → throw
			<code>Ephemeral keypair funding failed after 3 retries: …</code>
			(headless surfaces as <code>Audit failed: …</code>)
		</li>
		<li>Keys never persisted to disk or logged</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="router">Invoke / poll constants</h2>
	<p>Module <code>router.ts</code> — <code>invokeContract()</code> never throws; always returns typed <code>InvokeResult</code>:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><code>BASE_FEE = '100'</code></li>
		<li><code>TX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30</code> on the built transaction</li>
		<li>Poll <code>getTransaction</code>: <strong>20 × 1000ms</strong> → <code>TIMEOUT</code></li>
		<li>
			<code>broadcasted</code> is true only when <code>sendTransaction</code> was called
			successfully. A hash may still exist on <code>SEND_ERROR</code> (local envelope
			hash) with <code>broadcasted: false</code> — check both fields.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="modules">Key modules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><code>keypair_factory.ts</code> — ephemeral keys, never persisted</li>
		<li><code>type_gen.ts</code> — baseline + attack <code>ScVal</code>s from XDR types</li>
		<li><code>router.ts</code> — <code>invokeContract()</code> lifecycle</li>
		<li><code>trace_analyzer.ts</code> — AUTH / CONTRACT / CONTEXT / OBJECT / STORAGE / WASM_VM / …</li>
		<li><code>result_parser.ts</code> — maps traces → VulnerabilitySignal + Severity</li>
		<li><code>reporter.ts</code> — <code>KYF-NNN</code> IDs, verification transaction sample</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="fixtures">Fixtures</h2>
	<p>
		Repo <code>test-fixtures/</code> includes an intentionally vulnerable access-control
		contract and a composite UDT fixture for controlled Testnet demos — not production code.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<code>intentionally-vulnerable-contract</code> — <code>set_admin_value</code> without
			<code>require_auth</code> vs secure twin; name chosen to match admin patterns.
		</li>
		<li>
			<code>composite-udt-fixture</code> — nested structs/unions for recursive type_gen coverage.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Classify outcomes with <a href={withBase('/findings')}>Findings &amp; signals</a>. Stuck?
		<a href={withBase('/troubleshooting')}>Troubleshooting</a>.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
